# Sioona UI / App Router

Tokens, typography, Title Case / verb+noun labels, empty states, and focus rings live in `geist-design-system.mdc` — follow that; do not invent a parallel system.

**Colors:** prefer semantic `sio-*` / `--sio-*` (intent) over primitive `ds-*` / `--ds-*`. Primitives stay in `globals.css` as the alias source only. See geist-design-system “Token layers.”

## Structure

- Wrap pages in `AppShell` with a Title Case title + sentence-case subtitle
- Reuse signal chrome via `SignalStatus` / `SignalScoreChip` / `SignalTypeChip` / `SignalUser` (mappings in `format.ts`); colored `SignalBadge` only for taxonomy / legacy marks (lead=blue, retention=amber, upsell=teal — via `sio-signal-*` when styling in CSS)

## Reuse before inventing

From `globals.css`: `.panel`, `.btn-primary`, `.btn-secondary`, `.btn-tertiary`, `.input-field`, `.link-accent`, typography role classes (already on `sio-*` semantics).

- `"use client"` only for interactive controls (forms, feedback, buttons that mutate)
- Icons: `@phosphor-icons/react/ssr` — Bold for primary nav / key actions; Regular for dense chrome (queues, pagers, spinners)

## Serving Insights

Partner review is Feedback, Recommended Actions, and Why This Fired, then the weekly score on Eval. Do not restyle chips, radii, or the sidebar system. Do not add Auth0, live webhooks, or outbound send.

- **Transcript:** visible beside those cards when the review pane is at least `48rem` (a normal laptop with the sidebar open). Evidence quote is highlighted. Open Conversation is hidden at that width. Below that, Open Conversation and the quote open the drawer.
- **Review cards:** Feedback (Correct / Incorrect / Partially correct, note, Ground Truth in the header), then Recommended Actions (draft, Copy Reply, Run Actions, retention email), then Why This Fired. Nothing is sent.
- **Live export:** the default vault is Partner Demo forced open with Zerodha_batch_02 only. Sample is hidden there. Uploaded Chats stays off until the user has uploaded files; then those files are listed, with no “No files uploaded” line. When a non-showcase upload is loaded (chats present, not a filename-only landing), hide Reset, Run Partner Demo, and the Sample vault row. Partner Demo stays forced open. A weekly `?file=` that is not loaded does not hide Sample when uploaded files are already listed. The Insights list header shows Upload & Detect (light secondary button) to the right of “Conversation that needs your attention”; it opens Upload and does not wipe Partner Demo. Insights queue metrics stay open on the Partner Demo pack. The sidebar footer always shows Help, Guidance, Feedback, and the user account.
- **Copy:** Insights empty states and upload helpers say review five chats, mark the ones we got right, the weekly score is on Eval, and nothing is sent. Do not use keep-set, upsert, Day-1 replace, external id, or SignalScore in those helpers.
- **No Shadow Mode banner:** Never render an Insights status, warning, or tip that says “Shadow Mode — Confirm or correct detections. Replies are drafts only; nothing is sent.” Do not reintroduce `InsightsShadowTip` or that dismissible bar. That explanation stays in Help.
- **Empty / asleep:** a vault mismatch offers one next click (upload this week’s export). When the score service is asleep and uploaded chats are still loaded, Insights keeps the last queue counts, says the weekly score is waiting, and offers one Retry. An empty score queue is not finished work in that case. The Conversations cell shows the coverage share (chats with a signal / total) with the circle arrow.

## Next.js 15

- `params` and `searchParams` are Promises — `await` them
- Server Components read store; client components `fetch` APIs then `router.refresh()`
- Keep data routes `dynamic = "force-dynamic"` when reading the file store
